    "system": "Selex",
    "band": "C",
    "dualPol": true,
    "since": "2013",
    "towerM": 28,
    "text": {
      "en": "Stands at about 1,115 m in the forests of the Haute-Loire near La Chaise-Dieu; a radar has stood here since 1996. It watches the Massif Central and Cévennes-type downpours up to 180 km away. Because nearby trees keep growing, a new 50 m tower, France's tallest for a weather radar, is being built in 2026."
    },
