    "band": "C",
    "dualPol": true,
    "since": "2004",
    "towerM": 24,
    "text": {
      "en": "Stands at Météo-France's site in Trappes, south-west of Paris, and watches the Île-de-France region. Installed in 2004, it was the first dual-polarisation radar in France and served as the test bed for the polarimetric rain products later used across the network."
    },
